Which phases a wave gets: ⚠gate or advisory → a b c d e; NO-gate plain → a d e. EVERY wave has e: the production
close when it deploys, else the mini merge close; d always ends with `Next phase: e`, e with `none`. A gate PASS skips c;
c always goes back to b (advisory gate: c → d, no re-gate). Every prompt is SELF-CONTAINED: it opens with the §7 first line and the 3-line MAIN-THREAD
GUARD note, carries only what its phase needs and ends with the PHASE CLOSE lines; a phase never continues
into the next one in the same session.
Rules when instantiating:
- Every {{placeholder}} filled with REAL data from the analysis: exact task IDs, exact commands that exist in
  that repo, exact paths. Never invent.
- Phase a keeps the core sections in this order: GOAL · TASKS · SCOPE · LOOP · (VISUAL CHECK on UI waves only,
  between LOOP and WORKFLOW) · WORKFLOW · GUARDRAILS & PHASE CLOSE. SCOPE embeds the Step 3 investigation (the
  executing session never re-derives file lists). WORKFLOW is ALWAYS present and opens with AGENT BUDGET &
  ROLES, then one `## Executor brief` per task pre-filled from SCOPE (FILES, DOD-SLICE, FORBIDDEN) with
  placeholders for what the orchestrator completes in session (DELIVERABLE, DESIGN DECISIONS, STOP IF), closed
  by the single `## Simplifier brief` (pre-filled, ≤20 lines). Never emit a WORKFLOW where the main session
  implements first, where an executor self-approves, where the diff is audited by the executor's own tier,
  or whose agents add up to more than 20 in ONE phase session.
- Tiers: executors are `adcm-toolkits:executor` (`sonnet`) on NO-gate waves and `executor` + `model: opus` on
  ⚠gate waves; `adcm-toolkits:executor-frontend` replaces `executor` on UI and frontend-code waves (the wave
  loads design skills OR the task's FILES are frontend app code: components, pages, hooks/composables, client
  services/stores; cost: the `frontend-design` preload, ~3.1k tokens). Auditors are `adcm-toolkits:auditor`
  with `opus` until the quota of 10 per session (reserved: the simplify pass in a, the verifier in b), then
  `model: sonnet`. The doc-sync executor and the delivery `adcm-toolkits:courier` are `sonnet` ALWAYS.
  `model` explicit on every call or an `adcm-toolkits:*` type — a per-call `model` overrides the type's
  default; types fix the TOOL SET, the tier rules still set the model.
- The Reuse and Map lines in SCOPE are COPIED from the task's card in detailed-plan.md, never derived here; the
  executor brief repeats the comment ban in ONE line (full policy: detailed-plan §0).
- SCOPE budget UNCHANGED: ~15 lines per task (hard cap 25 for legitimately multi-file tasks), ≤60 per wave —
  the reuse verdict and the Map line live INSIDE the ~15. Overflow stays in the task's Scope manifest card;
  compress with brace-globs (`bold/{A,B,C}.tsx`) before dropping content.
- Gate reports: `{{docs_dir}}/qa/gate-{{wx}}.md` with the wave id in lowercase (existing convention), later rounds
  `qa/gate-{{wx}}-r<n>.md`, post-prod `qa/gate-{{wx}}-postprod.md` (`{{wx}}` = the wave id in lowercase).
- plan-audit seals every heading block naming the wave, these §7 phase prompts included: it runs AFTER the §7 prompts
  are written and BEFORE they are rendered or handed to the owner (skill Step 6b); phase a step 0 only checks the seal.
- Same-phase rule (all phases): a phase that cannot finish hands off to ITSELF — `Result: partial | fail` and `Next
  phase:` = that same phase, never `none` (`none` means the wave is finished and the digest refuses its prompt).
- Budget per prompt: a ≤170 lines, b–e ≤90 lines each, before the SCOPE and checklist content is inlined.
