# LOOP
brief → execute (sub-agent) → verify (YOU run the DoD-slice) → fix → repeat, then ONE simplify pass → re-verify. Max 5
rounds. The executor's 2nd failure of the SAME DoD line moves the task one tier up as a NEW agent with the attempt log
({{sonnet → opus → you | opus → you on ⚠gate waves}}); 3 attempts on the SAME failure without converging → stop and report
(never degrade tests, never mark done what isn't). The simplify pass consumes no round: a FULL DoD-auto failure after it
gets ONE fix round to the SAME simplifier (SendMessage), a second one reverts to the checkpoint, logged. A `RULE-OF-TWO`
line naming only files of this SCOPE → amend the briefs and extract in-wave (helper first, consumers after, serialized);
any file outside → handoff `Reuse:` follow-up. Never improvise. {{Wave-specific failure policy: flaky checks, early stop.}}

# VISUAL CHECK (mandatory if the wave touches UI: .pug/.html/.scss/.css/components)
grep + build prove the code is THERE, not that it LOOKS right. Before marking a UI task completed, DELEGATE capture AND
judgement to an `adcm-toolkits:researcher` (`sonnet`, 1 of the 20; when the DoD names the VISUAL CHECK,
`executor-frontend` captures it itself — never both): headless Chrome against a local server (full env) or the deployed URL,
`node {{repo}}/scripts/shot.{{cjs|mjs}} <url> <out.png> [lang] [width]` {{or: the FIRST UI task creates the helper}},
desktop (≥1280) AND mobile (375), both languages if i18n; it RETURNS findings (width, i18n, overlaps, design-system
fonts/colors) plus the PNG paths. Sub-agents return `MEDIA: unsent: <paths>` (they cannot send). The main session sends
unsent paths with SendUserFile by path WITHOUT opening them (load the tool with ToolSearch `select:SendUserFile`). Judging
screenshots is always a sub-agent's job (capture researcher, executor-frontend VISUAL CHECK, auditor); the guard denies image reads on the main thread. Keep the paths for the handoff.

