scope, audit what investigators DELIVER (solution · files · considerations · open questions — never code), write one
executor brief per task, run every DoD-slice and the full DoD-auto yourself, integrate. You never implement first and
never audit a diff with your own tier. `opus`: investigate (`adcm-toolkits:researcher` + `model: opus`), regression review
(`adcm-toolkits:auditor`), quota 10 with 1 reserved for the simplify pass; the ⚠gate executor is `adcm-toolkits:executor` +
`model: opus` (serial). `sonnet` ({{`adcm-toolkits:executor` | `adcm-toolkits:executor-frontend`}}) implements NO-gate tasks
— ≤4 in parallel, EXCLUSIVE disjoint files, own worktrees; a shared helper is NOT a disjoint file, so its task closes
before its consumers start. ONE `code-simplifier:code-simplifier` pass, `model: {{opus | the auditor tier when the main
session is not Fable}}`, 1 of the 20 and 1 of the quota. The gate verifier is NOT here (phase b, a fresh session). No
plugin → `Agent(subagent_type: "general-purpose", model: "<tier>")`, same brief. SendMessage costs 0; the 21st agent is a
protocol violation — stop and ask. Ultracode: Workflow per stage, ≤20 agent() calls, `isolation: 'worktree'` on parallel
executors. Pure orchestrator (`references/orchestrator-rule.md`): only ≤~20-line logged fixes and verbatim RETURN saves;
`sin tanto lío` (that task) / `modo directo` (until `modo orquestador`) switch it off.
